Patch 0077: the EE per-dispatch path (and the first part of the IOP thread).
What: checkpointDue/accountCycles (EeScheduler) and advanceEeTimers/creditEeTimers (PS2Memory) are inline in
their headers, so the fast path of every guest dispatch has no cross-unit calls (the slow path is the new
checkpointDueSlow); PS2Runtime::findFunction does hasFunction+lookupFunction in one table access, used by
the scheduler run loop and by dispatchGuestBranch for calls. Statements and order are unchanged.
This patch also carries the first part of the IOP thread (off by default: DON_IOP_THREAD=0 or unset keeps the IOP
inline on the EE thread): the worker thread, its hand-off in flushIopDebt and the queue of the IOP's effects on the EE
(ps2_runtime.*, ps2_iop_host.*). Patch 0078 adds the rest (thread name, DON_IOP_STRESS_US, SPU2 thread hooks).
Verified: perf_fight state hash identical to the pre-patch run (a71d52ac...906e5); GameThread CPU ms per blank
17.83 (baseline binary) -> 9.67 (this tree, which also holds the other sprint changes; not attributable alone).
Based on work/wip-2026-10-18/scheduler (earlier unfinished change), original to this project.

